<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Parihaspora</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">8th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> · Also known as Parihasapura</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Parihaspora was a city founded in the 8th century by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lalitaditya-muktapida">Lalitaditya Muktapida</a>, king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashmir">Kashmir</a>, on a plateau near modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srinagar">Srinagar</a>. It served as his capital and was filled with temples, monasteries and a great stupa. Later kings removed its materials, and only foundations and scattered ruins survive.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/parihaspora.jpg" alt="Parihaspora" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rayan Naqash · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ancient_Ruins_at_Parihaspora_01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
